    },
    {
      "post_id": "553241650307555328",
      "text": "@davegantly which kind of brings us back to his point? No one should be made to silently accept what they believe to be fundamentally wrong",
      "timestamp": "Thu Jan 08 17:27:42 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.5324065740252774e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "553191982450106368",
      "text": "@Baggerandy I was a fan, on the whole, but listening to him drunk on the glee of war, was hard. He gloats that oil was worth it @stephenfry",
      "timestamp": "Thu Jan 08 14:10:21 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.531914570464133e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "553231481628549121",
      "text": "@steviep56 I would agree with him, but he used his position to forward a neo con agenda that didn't consider any of the possible outcomes.",
      "timestamp": "Thu Jan 08 16:47:18 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.532308152458977e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "553246536566865920",
      "text": "@steviep56 Not comparable, but yes.  I also wouldn't compare the PM of GB in the 30s to a journalist in the 90s/00s. Hitler was unknown then",
